Z||000002||pHoOl||04-13-2001||10:33 PM||||How much did it cost in parts, and how long did it take to set up?  <P>Directions maybe?  i've seen more and more people doing this, and I LIKE!!!<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who can't outrun the cops.<P>AIM: phool88fiero<P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||grinthock||04-14-2001||09:41 AM||||Well my web site gives 90% of the info, cost?  The FILTER is what cost me the most, around $80....  it's a HUGE K&N...<BR> <A HREF="http://grinthock.2y.net/87intake.html" TARGET=_blank>http://grinthock.2y.net/87intake.html</A> <P>  Basically you gotta rip out the entire system... EVERYTHING!  Then you need to create the basic pipe, as I did, then drill a hole into it for the MAT sensor, then weld the nut to the pipe to hold the MAT in, then you need a silicon peice to hold the pipe on (for 3" intake use), mount the filter to the bottom of that pipe we just created.  You also need a oil breather to install in the location of the old breather pipe (that's the black pipe that goes from the rubber hose to the back of your plenum) I used the exising pipe, CUT and put the breather on it.<P>That's it, it's alot easier than you think, took us 3 hours but 2 of that was removing all the old crap.<P><BR>Anyone in the Toronto area who wants to see it is welcome to email and we can set something up, it's also an excuse to talk fiero's.... <P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by pHoOl:<BR><B>How much did it cost in parts, and how long did it take to set up?  <P>Directions maybe?  i've seen more and more people doing this, and I LIKE!!!<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||grinthock||04-14-2001||06:17 PM||||Just an UPDATE!  So everyone knows I did run into a problem, it seems that the Torshion Bar that holds up the trunk IS getting in the way, we couldn't re-fab the pipe enough without putting a MASSIVE bend in it, so we are going to REMOVE the torsion bar and put in a gas strut||||reg||4
Z||000005||pHoOl||04-14-2001||11:15 PM||||Question for you about the intake......<P>someone on this board had a sheet where they described 10 cheap ways to improve performance.  Dont' remember who it was.  They said to take the cover off the intake and look inside.  They then said to take a screwdriver or chisel and take out all of the plastic wall that is right there because it restricts airflow.<P>i took a look at mine, and i believe that what they are talking about is a splashguard.  Am I correct?  Cause i know that GM doesn't put in any parts that aren't necessary, too costly<BR><P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who can't outrun the cops.<P>AIM: phool88fiero<P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Nashco||04-14-2001||11:32 PM||||From what I've heard, the main reason this plastic is there is for noise reduction.  Just like any modern cars, any noise that can be reduced easily is.  The intake noise is pretty funky after you remove this plastic, but you have better air flow, according the supporters of the plastic bashing.<P>Just compare it to noise reducers in a normal intake hose on any normal car today.  Most people looking for performance remove them immediately because they have no performance gains and they don't mind the noise after it's removed.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000007||grinthock||04-15-2001||07:57 AM||||<BR>But honestly if actually sounds better, it's WAY lounder in the cabin than it was before, outside it's a bit louder.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Nashco:<BR><B>From what I've heard, the main reason this plastic is there is for noise reduction.  Just like any modern cars, any noise that can be reduced easily is.  The intake noise is pretty funky after you remove this plastic, but you have better air flow, according the supporters of the plastic bashing.<P>Just compare it to noise reducers in a normal intake hose on any normal car today.  Most people looking for performance remove them immediately because they have no performance gains and they don't mind the noise after it's removed.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||14
Z||000008||fyerstarter||04-15-2001||01:44 PM||||*Sniff* *Sniff* Do I smell a rat? *Sniff* I believe that I do. Funny that your "custom" fabricated intake setup bears a remarkable similarity to my sub $100 Autozone Civic Intake setup detailed in this thread: <BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/009138.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/009138.html</A>    <P>Even down to the decklid support hitting, and the ugly mismatching blue silicon piece which just happens to come as part of the kit.<P>Or did you just think that blue was a complimenting color to red?<P>I belong to a few 3d animation and digital art related forums as well and it seems that people are always inclined to claim they did more work than they actually did. It's a strange phenomenon indeed. <P>And $80 for a filter! You my friend were ripped off   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><p>[This message has been edited by fyerstarter (edited 04-15-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||grinthock||04-15-2001||02:02 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fyerstarter:<BR><B>*Sniff* *Sniff* Do I smell a rat? *Sniff* I believe that I do. Funny that your "custom" fabricated intake setup bears a remarkable similarity to my sub $100 Autozone Civic Intake setup detailed in this thread: <BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/009138.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/009138.html</A>    <P>Even down to the decklid support hitting, and the ugly mismatching blue silicon piece which just happens to come as part of the kit.<P>Or did you just think that blue was a complimenting color to red?<P>I belong to a few 3d animation and digital art related forums as well and it seems that people are always inclined to claim they did more work than they actually did. It's a strange phenomenon indeed. <P>And $80 for a filter! You my friend were ripped off    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>[This message has been edited by fyerstarter (edited 04-15-2001).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>FIRST of all I do'nt see where this attack came from, not called for dude.  This was custom, I mean there are only so many ways to build it...  Honestly I am not sure on the cost of the filter the whole thing cost me around $80 for parts and stuff like that.    2nd, we built it from scratch, designed it in the shop, ourselves, with no help and I hadn't even seen that thread before.  I wanted something that nobody else had that we did here, not something off the shelf... So that's what we did...    2ND the blue peice DID come from a CIVIC kit that we took parts OUT OF...  The pipe itself was a UBEND that we cut... <P>Before you go bashing people, watch your mouth, ask questions.  And do me a favor, don't goto any shows that I goto.<P>And for the record, we designed every part ourselves the only STOCK part was the blue joiner and the filter||||reg||1
Z||000010||fyerstarter||04-15-2001||02:21 PM||||Is that what "we" did? Looks like your friend is the one doing all the work in those pics. The whole thing cost you $80 or something? Since you were so intimitely involved in this project I would imagine you would know how much the parts cost. <P>&lt;<B>"I wanted something that nobody else had that we did here, not something off the shelf... "</B><P>Well I have an indentical setup. And it's made from parts of the shelf   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Maybe your friend who did all the work just ran down to Autozone and "custom fabricated" the parts while you were inside getting a beer? :P<P>Na, if you say you made it all yourself I believe you. I'll post a pic of mine in a few days and then you will see why I was sceptical. They are identical! But who knows, stranger things have happened. <P>Peace, and enjoy your intake  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><p>[This message has been edited by fyerstarter (edited 04-15-2001).]||||reg||1
